    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0476" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51ForcedLoan,1926/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-25T15:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                                1926—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 25—1:34
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. My 6, January 24, 3 p.m. Commercial attaché has telegraphed his Department
                    fully with request to give you copy.</p>
                <p>Spanish Minister<anchor n="16" xml:id="d203-f1"/> informs me that he and those of
                    his colleagues whose countries have had treaties explicitly exempting their
                    nationals from forced loans are jointly protesting accordingly.</p>
                <p>I have as yet received no communication from Foreign Office on the subject, but I
                    addressed a formal note to Minister for Foreign Affairs this morning, making
                    provisional reservations against application to American citizens so as to
                    permit whatever action you may instruct me to take.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d203-f1" n="16" xml:id="d203-f1-content">
                <p>Cristobal Fernandez Vallin, dean of the diplomatic corps.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
